# /new-component-preview

## Not available with plain partials

This project was set up with `--components=none` (plain ERB partials), and
Lookbook previews are built on component classes (`ViewComponent::Preview`).
There is nothing for a preview class to render.

What to do instead:

- **Check a partial visually:** render it on the page that uses it and cover it
  with a request or system spec (`/new-system-spec`, or `/new-spec`).
- **Want a component library with previews?** Re-run buildmate with
  `--components=view_component` (or `phlex`) and add the `lookbook` gem; this
  skill then generates Lookbook previews. Ignore `.claude/patterns/{{ 'patterns/lookbook-patterns.md' | installed(stack) }}`
  until then.
